#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kbrgb — control the Predator PHN16S-71 4-zone keyboard RGB (ENEK5130 i2c-HID).

Protocol credit: cleyton1986/predator-sense (hid_rgb.rs) and the
Linuwu-Sense community research it builds on.

Usage:
  kbrgb RRGGBB                  one static color, all zones
  kbrgb C1 C2 C3 C4             one static color per zone (left to right)
  kbrgb theme                   paint zones from the current omarchy theme
  kbrgb off                     all zones dark (also stops any effect)
  kbrgb restore                 reapply last setting (controller forgets on power-off)
  kbrgb <preset name>           run a preset from presets.conf (case insensitive)

Effects (animated, run until replaced):
  kbrgb breathe [C]             breathing fade in/out
  kbrgb rainbow                 all zones cycle the color wheel together
  kbrgb wave                    moving rainbow across the zones
  kbrgb snake [C]               scanner: bright head ping-pongs, tail fades
  kbrgb meteor [C]              comet sweeping one way with wrap-around tail
  kbrgb police [C1 C2]          alternating zone strobe (default red/blue)
  kbrgb sparkle [C...]          random zones twinkle and fade (default theme)
  kbrgb fire                    flickering embers
  kbrgb heartbeat [C]           double-pulse rhythm
  kbrgb aurora                  slow northern-lights hue drift
  kbrgb ocean                   rolling blue swells across zones
  kbrgb lava                    slow oozing magma
  kbrgb matrix                  green digital rain
  kbrgb candle                  cozy warm flicker
  kbrgb storm                   dark night sky with lightning strikes
  kbrgb disco                   beat-cut random zones and colors
  kbrgb duel [C1 C2]            two comets bouncing from opposite ends
  kbrgb shadow [C]              lit field with a roaming dark gap
  kbrgb ripple [C]              breathing that flows zone to zone
  kbrgb chase [C]               hard marquee: one zone at a time
  kbrgb strobe [C]              party strobe (use responsibly)
  kbrgb cpuheat                 zones show CPU temp: green=cool red=hot
  kbrgb battery                 4-zone battery bar, breathes while charging
  kbrgb prism                   flowing ripple that shifts hue every sweep
  kbrgb glitch [C]              stable color with cyberpunk malfunction bursts
  kbrgb eruption                smoldering volcano with violent eruptions
  kbrgb redalert [C]            klaxon ramp-and-cut alarm sweep
  kbrgb supernova               slow charge-up, explosion, fading embers
  kbrgb shockwave [C]           fast bright front slams across, then silence
  kbrgb load                    live load meter: CPU left half, GPU right
  kbrgb clock                   ambient hue that follows the time of day
  kbrgb netpulse                network meter: download cyan, upload orange
  kbrgb pomo [MIN]              pomodoro timer, default 25 minutes

Reactive effects (read your typing; needs the "input" group, see README):
  kbrgb typewriter [C]          every keystroke glows the board brighter
  kbrgb keyflash [C]            the zone under each key flashes and spills
  kbrgb wpmheat [WPM]           typing speed as heat, red at WPM (def. 96)
  kbrgb zen [C]                 fades out after -s idle seconds, keys wake it
  kbrgb flow [WPM]              wpmheat + zen: speed heat that sleeps with you

EC-native effects (one write, the controller animates on its own — zero CPU):
  kbrgb native <name> [C]       breathe neon wave zoom meteor twinkle
  kbrgb native list             native effect names + which take a color

Flags:
  -b N    brightness percent 0-100 (default 100)
  -s N    effect cycle period in seconds (default per effect);
          for native effects: EC speed 0-10 (default 5)
  -r      reverse the native wave (direction byte; other effects ignore it)

Tools:
  kbrgb list                    list every effect name
  kbrgb demo                    tour all effects, ~4s each (Ctrl-C stops)
  kbrgb probe                   guided hardware diagnostic — run this to
                                report support for a new laptop model
  kbrgb status                  show device, saved state, daemon state

Colors are RRGGBB hex. Effect defaults come from the active omarchy theme
when available, with built-in fallbacks otherwise.
"""
import fcntl, glob, math, os, random, re, select, signal, struct, sys, time
from collections import deque

# NOTE (verified on PHN16S-71 hardware, two machines):
# - brightness byte range is 0-100 (predator-sense shipped the same fix
#   in v0.2.27 after our report)
# - mask 0x0f writes all four zones at once and works fine; an earlier
#   "0x0f is broken" claim was a test artifact (packet sent at brightness
#   15 before the 0-100 range was understood)
# packet: a4 21 mode bright speed dir R G B mask 00 (mode 0x02 = static;
# native-effect mode bytes below, discovered in DAMX PR #213)
HIDIOCSFEATURE_11 = 0xC00B4806
ZONES = [0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08]
ZONE_ALL = 0x0F

# EC-native onboard effects: one feature report, hardware loops it forever.
# Mode byte mapped by abduvaliy-hbai (DAMX PR #213) on a Nitro ANV16S-41,
# confirmed identical on the PHN16S-71 after his 0x07/0x09 retest (see
# PROTOCOL.md). Hostile bytes deliberately unreachable:
# 0x01/0x03 off, 0x06 flash, 0x08 glitchy, 0x0c freezes the lighting.
